onance\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V06 -->\n```\n\nElectronic, vibrational, rotational, Raman, hyperfine, nuclear, magnetic resonance, acoustic, plasma.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Physical Properties\n\n| Property | Value | Unit | Conditions | Evidence | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| atomicWeight | NOT_APPLICABLE | dimensionless / text | See source | NOT_APPLICABLE | CIAAW-2024 |\n| electronConfiguration | [Rn] 5f12 7s2 | dimensionless / text | See source | REPORTED | PUBCHEM-PERIODIC |\n| electronegativity | 1.3 | Pauling | See source | REPORTED | PUBCHEM-PERIODIC |\n| firstIonizationEnergy | 6.5 | eV | See source | REPORTED | PUBCHEM-PERIODIC |\n| phase | Solid | dimensionless / text | Source standard state; verify temperature and pressure for reuse | REPORTED | PUBCHEM-PERIODIC |\n| meltingPoint | 1800 | K | See source | REPORTED | PUBCHEM-PERIODIC |\n| boilingPoint | UNAVAILABLE | K | See source | UNAVAILABLE | UNAVAILABLE |\n| density | UNAVAILABLE | g/cm3 | Source reference conditions; consult element page | UNAVAILABLE | UNAVAILABLE |\n| oxidationStates | +3 | dimensionless / text | See source | REPORTED | PUBCHEM-PERIODIC |\n\nAbundances remain UNAVAILABLE pending source-specific curation. Standard atomic weight is dimensionless; isotope mass numbers are not substituted for it. For helium, a melting point needs pressure-specific qualification.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Electrical Properties\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V08 -->\n```\n\nConductivity, resistivity, permittivity, dielectric loss.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Magnetic Properties\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V09 -->\n```\n\nSusceptibility, ordering, permeability, magnetic moments.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Thermal and Thermodynamic Properties\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V10 -->\n```\n\nMelting, boiling, heat capacity, conductivity, diffusivity.\n\n---\n\n# 13. Mechanical Properties\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V11 -->\n```\n\nModulus, strength, hardness, toughness, creep, fatigue.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Phase, Pressure and Environment\n\n